# RFC #362 desktop.11 (Windows distribution patch, also valid upstream):
#
# A fresh window waits out a dead window's lease instead of stalling on it.
#
# Reopening a project within ~60 s of an ungraceful window close (app
# crash, killed browser tab, VM snapshot) answered with a hard error card:
# "This project is open in another window", needing a manual reload the
# user can only answer by waiting anyway. Three sandbox sessions tripped
# over this while doing unrelated work — it is the top papercut on reopen.
#
# The lease holder is usually already gone; the lease just has not expired
# yet. The workspace init now retries quietly every 3 s for up to ~75 s
# when, and only when, the refusal is project_open_elsewhere on a fresh
# window (reloaded tabs keep their own existing retry in creationClient;
# storage_busy keeps its backoff; every other error still fails at once).
# While waiting, the loading screen says what is happening with a countdown
# and keeps Reconnect / Back to canvas home as explicit exits — the
# failure-state rule: every in-progress state has a way out. If the lease
# really belongs to a live window, retries exhaust and the original error
# card shows, so a genuine conflict is never masked.
#
# Lease semantics are unchanged: no takeover, no shortened lease, no
# change to sessions storage. This is initialization retry + presentation.
# The desktop side complements it: service.py journals renderer sessions
# and releases them at next launch, so an app crash + restart opens at
# once (see tests/test_transport.py).
